   "issues": [],
   "scene": "OddSquares"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover_end",
   "t": 148.945,
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "OddSquares"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover",
   "t": 150.645,
   "duration": 19.691,
   "text": "So adding the odd numbers in order is adding the Ls in order. After n Ls, the square has side n. So the first n odd numbers add up to n times n. The question mark can go. We write n times n as n squared, n with a small two. The brace marks the n odd numbers, and the dots mean: and so on, in order.",
   "bookmarks": {
    "build": 154.579,
    "done": 157.12,
    "sq": 162.238,
    "dots": 165.832
   },
   "scene": "OddSquares"
